{"defects":[{"file":"app/form/_actions/form-actions.ts","line":33,"end_line":33,"in_diff":true,"hunk":"new:32-33","category":"potential-issue","severity":"major","quick_win":true,"title":"Align the upload allowlist with the form category names","body":"The newly mandatory uploads for parents, marriage certificate, and students cannot obtain upload tickets. The allowlist accepts `doc_pai`, `doc_mae`, `certidao_casamento`, and `aluno_<n>_(rg|certidao)`, while the rendered controls request `rg_pai`, `rg_mae`, `certidao`, `rg_aluno_<n>`, and `certidao_nascimento_<n>`. `createUploadUrl` returns an error before the PUT, leaving required fields impossible to complete.","rule_ids":[],"also_applies":["app/form/_components/step-1-applicant.tsx:new:139-139","app/form/_components/step-1-applicant.tsx:new:146-146","app/form/_components/step-1-applicant.tsx:new:183-183","app/form/_components/step-1-applicant.tsx:new:190-190","app/form/_components/step-1-applicant.tsx:new:200-200","app/form/_components/step-1-applicant.tsx:new:207-207","app/form/_components/step-2-students.tsx:new:184-184","app/form/_components/step-2-students.tsx:new:191-191","app/form/_components/step-2-students.tsx:new:198-198","app/form/_components/step-2-students.tsx:new:205-205"],"guideline":null,"suggestion":null,"evidence":["Premise: app/form/_actions/form-actions.ts:32-33 only accepts the named fixed values or `aluno_<n>_(rg|certidao)` → Path: FileUpload calls createUploadUrl with the categories rendered in the parent/student controls → Verdict: those required uploads are rejected as an invalid category.","app/form/_components/step-1-applicant.tsx:143,187,204 → parent and marriage controls send `rg_pai`, `rg_mae`, and `certidao`.","app/form/_components/step-2-students.tsx:188,202 → student controls send `rg_aluno_<n>` and `certidao_nascimento_<n>`."]},{"file":"lib/validations/application-schema.ts","line":77,"end_line":77,"in_diff":true,"hunk":"new:77-77","category":"potential-issue","severity":"major","quick_win":false,"title":"Verify that required document paths refer to uploaded files","body":"Required arrays only prove that the client supplied a string beginning with `pending/`; they do not prove a successful upload. A direct Server Action caller can submit all required fields as distinct nonexistent `pending/<uuid>/...` paths. `fillDocumentSizes` turns each missing object into size 0 and the transaction persists them, so the application succeeds without the now-required evidence.","rule_ids":[],"also_applies":["lib/validations/application-schema.ts:new:84-84","lib/validations/application-schema.ts:new:91-91","lib/validations/application-schema.ts:new:94-94","lib/validations/application-schema.ts:new:99-99","lib/validations/application-schema.ts:new:119-119","lib/validations/application-schema.ts:new:130-130","lib/validations/application-schema.ts:new:36-37"],"guideline":null,"suggestion":null,"evidence":["Premise: lib/validations/application-schema.ts:20-25 accepts any nonempty `pending/` path without a storage lookup → Path: a caller invokes submitApplication with invented required paths → Verdict: successful submission can contain no uploaded document.","app/form/_actions/form-actions.ts:291-296 → missing storage objects are represented as `tamanho_bytes: 0`, not rejected.","app/form/_actions/form-actions.ts:209-214 → those rows are inserted whenever the arrays are nonempty."]},{"file":"lib/documents/issued-documents.ts","line":21,"end_line":35,"in_diff":true,"hunk":"new:1-64","category":"potential-issue","severity":"major","quick_win":false,"title":"Serialize issued-document version allocation","body":"Two simultaneous reissues for the same application and kind can both read the same latest version before either insert. Both then attempt `latest + 1`; the unique index makes one transaction fail instead of allocating the next monotonic version. The required concurrency-safe issuance therefore produces a user-visible emission error and leaves the second generated artifact compensated away.","rule_ids":[],"also_applies":["drizzle/0006_flimsy_spacker_dave.sql:new:1-40"],"guideline":null,"suggestion":null,"evidence":["Premise: lib/documents/issued-documents.ts:21-35 reads the latest version and inserts `latest + 1` without a row/advisory lock or atomic sequence allocation → Path: two concurrent persistIssuedDocument calls for identical applicationId/kind both observe version N → Verdict: both try N+1 and one violates the unique application/kind/version index.","drizzle/0006_flimsy_spacker_dave.sql:38 → the database uniqueness constraint detects the collision but does not serialize or retry allocation.",".compozy/tasks/donor-first-role-access/task_03.md:29 → the contract explicitly requires serialized version allocation per application."]},{"file":"app/admin/_actions/admin-actions.ts","line":534,"end_line":536,"in_diff":true,"hunk":"new:533-537","category":"potential-issue","severity":"major","quick_win":true,"title":"Handle the development bypass when recording an issued document","body":"The documented `AUTH_BYPASS=true` administrator has the all-zero façade ID and no `admin_users` row. Exporting a decision or contract passes that ID to `persistIssuedDocument`, but `issued_documents.issued_by` is a non-null foreign key to `admin_users`; the insert fails and the action reports that it could not register the issuance. This makes final-document export unusable in the supported development mode.","rule_ids":[],"also_applies":["app/admin/_actions/admin-actions.ts:new:786-790"],"guideline":null,"suggestion":null,"evidence":["Premise: app/admin/_actions/admin-actions.ts:534 passes `user.id` as `issuedBy` → Path: AUTH_BYPASS=true authenticates the façade user and exports a final document → Verdict: persistence uses an ID absent from admin_users and violates the issued_by foreign key.","lib/auth/bypass.ts:4-19 → the bypass ID is `00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000` and bypass does not query admin_users.","drizzle/0006_flimsy_spacker_dave.sql:35 → issued_by has a non-null foreign key to admin_users."]},{"file":"app/admin/solicitacoes/client.tsx","line":80,"end_line":99,"in_diff":true,"hunk":"new:69-107","category":"potential-issue","severity":"major","quick_win":false,"title":"Expose issued-document download in the Secretariat application view","body":"The Secretariat client renders only status, contact data, students, and decision date. It never calls `getCurrentIssuedDocuments` or `getIssuedDocumentUrl`, while the only IssuedDocuments component is mounted inside the Administrator ApplicationCard. Thus a Secretariat user has no application UI through which to consult or download an Administrator-issued decision or eligible contract.","rule_ids":[],"also_applies":["app/admin/_components/application-card.tsx:new:307-307"],"guideline":null,"suggestion":null,"evidence":["Premise: app/admin/solicitacoes/client.tsx:80-99 maps each Secretariat application to static operational fields only → Path: a Secretaria user opens /admin/solicitacoes after a document is issued → Verdict: no control invokes the available document-read/download actions.","app/admin/_components/issued-documents.tsx:4-13 → the only document UI calls the issuance actions.","app/admin/_components/application-card.tsx:307-310 → that component is mounted only by the Administrator card, not SecretariatApplicationsClient."]},{"file":"app/admin/solicitacoes/client.tsx","line":80,"end_line":99,"in_diff":true,"hunk":"new:69-107","category":"potential-issue","severity":"major","quick_win":false,"title":"Add the required Secretariat observation history and entry flow","body":"Although server actions for observations were added, neither the Secretariat client nor any other rendered admin component imports or calls them. A Secretaria user can therefore neither see the chronological internal history nor add an observation, leaving the operational workflow unavailable.","rule_ids":[],"also_applies":["app/admin/_actions/observation-actions.ts:new:1-34"],"guideline":null,"suggestion":null,"evidence":["Premise: app/admin/solicitacoes/client.tsx:80-99 renders the complete Secretariat application card without an observation section or action → Path: a Secretariat user follows up an application in the only role-specific solicitation UI → Verdict: the required read/create observation workflow is inaccessible.","rg `getApplicationObservations|addApplicationObservation` app → only app/admin/_actions/observation-actions.ts defines the actions; no component consumes them.",".compozy/tasks/donor-first-role-access/task_02.md:31 → Secretariat must be able to create/read chronological append-only observations."]}],"advisories":[],"suppressions":[{"file":"app/admin/_actions/admin-actions.ts","line":121,"hunk":"new:121-142","candidate":"Secretariat donor projection returns financial operational fields.","reason":"intentional","rule_ids":[],"note":"The inspected TechSpec explicitly allowlists frequency, duration, amount, payment details, reminder channel, location, donor observations, and enrollment date for Secretariat donors."},{"file":"app/admin/_actions/admin-actions.ts","line":795,"hunk":"new:794-823","candidate":"Current issued-document action returns documents to a pending application.","reason":"intentional","rule_ids":[],"note":"The action explicitly returns [] for pending applications and filters rejected applications to decisions, matching the final-document eligibility contract."}],"coverage":{"hunks":[{"file":".compozy/tasks/donor-first-role-access/_prd.md","hunk":"new:1-330","checks":["defect"],"outcome":"clear"},{"file":".compozy/tasks/donor-first-role-access/_tasks.md","hunk":"new:1-11","checks":["defect"],"outcome":"clear"},{"file":".compozy/tasks/donor-first-role-access/_techspec.md","hunk":"new:1-707","checks":["defect"],"outcome":"clear"},{"file":".compozy/tasks/donor-first-role-access/adrs/adr-001.md","hunk":"new:1-67","checks":["defect"],"outcome":"clear"},{"file":".compozy/tasks/donor-first-role-acc